# GitHub Issues

## Before substantive implementation

1. Check related issues (`gh issue list`; `gh issue view N` when relevant) for substantive, tracked work.
2. Prefer extending an existing issue over creating a duplicate.
3. Align implementation with issue acceptance criteria when an issue exists.

Tiny, self-contained fixes and read-only tasks do not need issue-tracker ceremony. Follow explicit user requests and other project policies when they require an issue.

## PRs

- Done → `Closes #N` · Partial/related → `Refs #N`
- Do **not** close until acceptance criteria are truly met (stubs ≠ done)

## Gaps discovered mid-work

Update issue body/checklist, comment, or reopen — do not silently diverge from the tracker.
